      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my bosch dishwasher is showing an e15 error code. i checked the manual but im not really sure what to do. how do i check the leak sensor and dry out the base?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The E15 code on a Bosch dishwasher indicates a water leak detected by the internal sensor, not necessarily a problem with the base itself. To address this, you should first check the hoses underneath the machine for cracks, kinks, or loose connections where they seal into the unit. If you suspect a leak at the drain filter or center sump, carefully remove the bottom rack and with a flashlight, wipe away any standing water to see if the sensor triggers a reset. If these steps don't resolve the issue, the leak sensor might be faulty or blocked by debris, requiring professional diagnosis.",
